        <body>
            <div xml:id="d637">

                <pb facs="0696" n="592" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg592"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Manchuria/65</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-03-17">March 17, 1932</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Belgian Ambassador said that his Government had received an invitation from
                    the new Manchurian State to recognize it, and asked me whether we had received
                    one and what we were going to do. I told the Ambassador that we had received one
                    and we did not intend to recognize it. I pointed out to him Article 2 of the
                    Nine-Power Treaty and said that, for myself, I was inclined to think that that
                    Article must be very carefully considered before we recognize the new Manchurian
                    State for it would seem, at first hand, to be a promise on our part, and by each
                    of the other signatories of the Nine-Power Treaty, not to make such a
                    recognition in such a case as was presented in Manchuria. The Ambassador said he
                    was very much interested because his country was also a signatory to the
                    Nine-Power Treaty.</p>
                <closer><signed>H[<hi rendition="#small-caps">enry</hi>] L. S[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">timson</hi>]</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
